# Modal sticky header / footer

Scrollable modals must keep **header** and **footer** fixed inside the panel. Only the **body** scrolls. Do not put `overflow-y-auto` on a wrapper that also contains the title or action buttons.

## Shell (required)

`Modal` panel is already `flex flex-col overflow-hidden`. Inside `children`:

```tsx
<Modal contentClassName="max-w-… max-h-[90vh]" …>
  <div className="flex min-h-0 flex-1 flex-col">
    <header className="shrink-0 border-b … px-6 py-4">
      {/* title / subtitle */}
    </header>
    <div className="min-h-0 flex-1 overflow-y-auto px-6 py-4">
      {/* scrollable fields */}
    </div>
    <footer className="flex shrink-0 justify-end gap-2 border-t … px-6 py-4">
      {/* cancel / apply */}
    </footer>
  </div>
</Modal>
```

Reference: `SettingsModal`, `DocumentSettingsModal`.

## Checklist

1. Panel has a height cap (`max-h-[90vh]` or equivalent) so overflow can occur.
2. Outer child: `flex min-h-0 flex-1 flex-col` (not `overflow-y-auto` on the whole thing).
3. Header + footer: `shrink-0` (optional `border-b` / `border-t`).
4. Body: `min-h-0 flex-1 overflow-y-auto`.
5. Short confirm dialogs with no long body may omit the scroll region, but still keep actions in a distinct footer if both title and buttons exist.

```text
❌ BAD — one overflow-y-auto wrapper around title + form + Apply
❌ BAD — sticky footer inside a scrolling parent (header still scrolls away)
✅ GOOD — flex column; only middle pane scrolls
✅ GOOD — SettingsModal / DocumentSettingsModal pattern
```

Prefer **English** in new code comments if Korean Unicode might corrupt.
